# Batch 10: the paper's input budget. 12 jobs = 4 arms x seeds 0-2, 150k, snapshots every 10k, one full checkpoint
# at 150k. Every arm is configs/batch9_c2_both_paper.json with only the fields below changed: the first 128 steps
# (1.28 ns) of all 60 PE trajectories, no offsets, no hold-out, 2-block increments critic, noise-use reward (min 0.5,
# weight 100), side chain of 2 blocks x 1024 chains, M 64, sigma units. NOT in the papers (the rewards).
# Training code and configs: commit 0f5ab71 on branch batch8-short-data (this file came in the commit after
# it; each run's provenance.json records the commit that ran).
#
# Batch 9's c2_both_paper (the same input, correlation reward on block lag 1) came out at D 1.68 x MD (all 60
# trajectories), err 38-160 %, var/MD 1.1-2.3, D/tgt 1.37-3.4: the model did not follow its own target, and the
# variance was too high. This batch separates the variance from the correlations, and replaces the one noisy block
# lag-1 target (180 pairs) with sub-block correlations (1260 pairs at lag 1).
#
#   arm (config batch10_<arm>.json)  departure from batch9_c2_both_paper
#   c2_both_paper_var                + variance reward (64-step block sums), weight 0.92
#   c2_noise_var_paper               correlation weight 0 (side chain kept, so blocks are still decoded) + variance
#                                    reward (block sums), weight 0.92
#   c2_noise_subcorr_var_paper       correlation weight 0 + sub-block correlation reward (16-step sub-blocks, lags 1-7),
#                                    weight 25 + variance reward on the 16-step sub-block sums, weight 1.5
#   c2_noise_subcorr_var_2p5ns       the previous arm on the first 256 steps (window_offset_max_steps 128), still 60
#                                    trajectories, no hold-out; weights 15 (sub-block) and 0.85 (variance)
#
# Weights: tools/variance_weight.py on each config, PE, freshly initialised models (seeds 0-2 x 3 side batches): the
# weight at which a term's gradient norm over G_z + G_Y equals that of the block lag-1 correlation term at weight 10.
# Medians, rounded to two figures (ranges over the 9 draws):
#   c2_both_paper_var, c2_noise_var_paper   variance 0.922 (0.85-1.09)               -> 0.92 (the two configs draw
#                                                                                       identical side batches)
#   c2_noise_subcorr_var_paper              variance 1.51 (1.40-1.88); sub-block 25.2 (21.7-33.9)   -> 1.5, 25
#   c2_noise_subcorr_var_2p5ns              variance 0.853 (0.77-1.13); sub-block 15.3 (13.7-20.1)  -> 0.85, 15
# At initialisation V_gen / V_target is 0.07-0.09 (block) and 0.05-0.07 (sub-block): the equality holds where the
# variance is far too low, as for Batch 9's 0.78 (measured on 80 ns, not reused here).
#
# Targets (dataset.json; measured on PE, all 60 trajectories):
#   region 0-128   block lag 1        -0.246  (180 pairs: one per trajectory and axis)
#                  block variance     9.835 sigma^2  (360 block sums)                     [c2_both_paper_var, c2_noise_var_paper]
#                  sub-block rho 1-7  -0.190 -0.024 -0.050 +0.020 -0.073 -0.001 +0.008
#                  pairs              1260   1080    900    720    540    360    180
#                  sub-block variance 3.492 sigma^2  (1440 sub-block sums)                [c2_noise_subcorr_var_paper]
#   region 0-256   block lag 1        -0.138  (pooled over the 64 block grids)
#                  sub-block rho 1-7  -0.196 -0.010 -0.040 +0.007 -0.040 +0.005 -0.030
#                  pairs              2700   2520   2340   2160   1980   1800   1620
#                  sub-block variance 3.523 sigma^2  (2880 sub-block sums)                [c2_noise_subcorr_var_2p5ns]
# The 80 ns values for comparison: block lag 1 -0.148, sum rho (1-3) -0.18.
# By the identity rho_B1 = sum_{d=1..7} (4 - |d - 4|) rho_d / (4 + 2 (3 rho_1 + 2 rho_2 + rho_3)) (sub-blocks of M/4;
# exact for a stationary series, tested), the sub-block targets imply a block lag 1 of -0.196 on 0-128 and -0.165 on
# 0-256, and by (1 + 2 rho_B1) / (1 + 2 rho_B1,80ns) a D of about 0.86 x and 0.95 x MD.
#
# PREDICTIONS
#   resume (batch10_resume.sub): if var/MD is still above 1.3 and err above 40 % at 150k, training length is not the
#     missing piece at this budget.
#   c2_both_paper_var: var/MD within 0.85-1.15; D then follows sum rho, expected 0.7-1.0 x depending on how far the
#     model moves toward the -0.246 target.
#   c2_noise_var_paper: var/MD near 1, sum rho about -0.05, D about 1.3 x.
#   c2_noise_subcorr_var_paper: var/MD near 1, block sum rho within 0.05 of the 80 ns value (-0.15), D within
#     0.85-1.15, typical err 15-25 %. Note: its targets imply block lag 1 -0.196, 0.048 from -0.148, so "within 0.05"
#     is met only if the model lands on or slightly short of its own targets; following them exactly gives D ~0.86 x.
#   c2_noise_subcorr_var_2p5ns: the same with a tighter spread (targets imply -0.165 and D ~0.95 x).
#
# Reading the results: the rewards train on block or sub-block variance and on rho (block lag 1, or sub-block lags
# 1-7, which fix block lag 1), so var/MD and rho(1-3) cannot judge these arms. Judge on err, D, the MSD ratio at
# 10-78 ns, sum rho(4-30) and the latent criteria (DC share, ACF at lag 100). All four arms train on all 60
# trajectories, so the held-out evaluation does not apply; read them on all 60. arm-eval's D_tgt reads
# corr_reward_targets (block lag 1); for the three arms with correlation weight 0 that is the data's block lag 1,
# not what the arm trains on (use -0.196 / -0.165 above for the sub-block arms).
# New metrics.jsonl columns: subcorr_error (sub-block arms); block_var_ratio and variance_penalty (all four arms;
# the ratio is of sub-block variances in the sub-block arms). corr_error is logged in every arm, also at weight 0.
#
# Disk: about 1.83 GB per run (latest.pt and full_150000.pt 375 MB each, fifteen 72 MB snapshots), 22 GB for 12 runs.
# Time: Batch 9's c2_both_paper ran at 0.071 s per iteration: about 3 h per run, up to about 10 h on the slowest GPUs.
# Submit from the repository root in /home:  condor_submit tools/chtc/batch10.sub

universe                  = container
container_image           = docker://pytorch/pytorch:2.5.1-cuda12.4-cudnn9-runtime
executable                = tools/chtc/run_train.sh
should_transfer_files     = YES
when_to_transfer_output   = ON_EXIT
checkpoint_exit_code      = 85

request_gpus              = 1
# The container's PyTorch (2.5.1, CUDA 12.4) has GPU code for compute capability 5.0-9.0 only;
# newer GPUs fail at the first CUDA call ('no kernel image is available'). 9.0 = H100, 8.9 = L40.
gpus_minimum_capability   = 7.0
gpus_maximum_capability   = 9.0
# gpu2008: its GPU fails every job at the first CUDA call (busy or unavailable), Nov 2026
requirements              = (Machine != "gpu2008.chtc.wisc.edu")
+WantGPULab               = true
+GPUJobLength             = "short"
request_cpus              = 2
request_memory            = 4GB
request_disk              = 5GB

arguments                 = $(ARM)_c$(Cluster)_seed$(SEED) $(SEED)
environment               = "MAX_HOURS=11 CONFIG=batch10_$(ARM).json"
transfer_input_files      = src, configs/batch10_$(ARM).json, data/cache/PE.npz
transfer_checkpoint_files = run_$(ARM)_c$(Cluster)_seed$(SEED)
transfer_output_files     = run_$(ARM)_c$(Cluster)_seed$(SEED)
log                       = logs/$(ARM)_c$(Cluster)_seed$(SEED).log
output                    = logs/$(ARM)_c$(Cluster)_seed$(SEED).out
error                     = logs/$(ARM)_c$(Cluster)_seed$(SEED).err

queue ARM, SEED from (
  c2_both_paper_var, 0
  c2_both_paper_var, 1
  c2_both_paper_var, 2
  c2_noise_var_paper, 0
  c2_noise_var_paper, 1
  c2_noise_var_paper, 2
  c2_noise_subcorr_var_paper, 0
  c2_noise_subcorr_var_paper, 1
  c2_noise_subcorr_var_paper, 2
  c2_noise_subcorr_var_2p5ns, 0
  c2_noise_subcorr_var_2p5ns, 1
  c2_noise_subcorr_var_2p5ns, 2
)
